@startuml architecture_failover
!include _style.puml

title Regional Failover & Fail-back (Route 53 health-checked)

participant "Browser" as b
participant "Route 53\nfailover record" as dns
participant "us-east-1\nPRIMARY" as east
participant "us-west-2\nSTANDBY" as west

== Steady state ==
b -> dns : resolve domain
dns -> east : health check /api/health = 200
b -> east : all traffic (writes here)
east -> west : S3 CRR + Litestream WAL (continuous)

== Primary fails ==
east -> dns : /api/health stops returning 200
note over dns : ~3 failed checks (~90s)\nmark PRIMARY unhealthy
dns -> west : promote SECONDARY
b -> west : traffic now served by west\n(Litestream has the replicated data)
note over b : RegionFailoverBanner shows\nduring the DNS gap, then clears

== Recovery / fail-back (GATED — manual) ==
east -> dns : /api/health healthy again
note over dns #FDECEC : ⚠ Auto-return to east would\nDISCARD writes made on west\n(CRR is east→west ONLY)
note over west, east #FDECEC : If west took writes during the outage:\nHOLD east, reconcile west→east\n(deploy/failover_control.sh), THEN release
dns -> east : traffic back to primary\n(only after reconcile, or if no west writes)

legend bottom
  Active/passive, single-writer SQLite — exactly one region writes at a time.
  Drill trigger: flip the primary health-check path to /api/profiles/ (401).
  Forward failover (east→west) VERIFIED 2026-10-27 (+ on the recreated
  Object-Lock buckets 2026-10-31). FAIL-BACK is gated/manual: CRR is one-way
  (east→west), so west's outage-window writes have no automatic path back —
  "no data divergence" on auto-fail-back is UNVERIFIED. See PHASE2_FAILOVER.md.
end legend

@enduml
